  <!-- SECTION 1 -->
  <a name="introduction"></a>
  <h1>1. INTRODUCTION & SYSTEM OVERVIEW</h1>
  <p>The Valdez Elementary School Portal is an integrated management platform designed to streamline school operations, automate student record management, facilitate parent/student academic tracking, and improve teacher-administrative workflows. The system is built on a React and Vite frontend framework backed by an Express Node.js server. A key feature of this project is its live database synchronization with a local Microsoft Excel spreadsheet (database.xlsx), making data administration accessible to school staff with minimal technical overhead.</p>
  
  <h3>Key Architectural Features:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><span class="strong-term">Node.js Server:</span> Express Node.js backend serves dynamic REST APIs and manages spreadsheet reading/writing.</li>
    <li><span class="strong-term">React Frontend:</span> React + Vite handles the web client interfaces using Vanilla CSS, ensuring rich styling, responsiveness, and premium dark/light mode aesthetics.</li>
    <li><span class="strong-term">Excel Database Synchronization:</span> Located in `server/data/database.xlsx`, the spreadsheet is the primary database. Any change in the Excel sheet reloads automatically in the web client, and any administrative update in the portal is written back directly to the Excel file.</li>
    <li><span class="strong-term">AI Companion Assistant:</span> Bella, an interactive animated cat chatbot mascot, is integrated to provide real-time Q&A on school metrics, using Gemini 1.5 Flash API with a localized fact-learning system.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- SECTION 2 -->
  <a name="running-project"></a>
  <h1>2. INSTALLATION & HOW TO RUN THE PROJECT</h1>
  <p>Follow these steps to set up and run the Valdez Elementary School Portal on a local computer:</p>
  
  <h2>Step 2.1: Verify Prerequisites</h2>
  <p>Ensure that Node.js (version 18 or higher) and npm are installed on your computer. You can verify this by running the following commands in your command prompt or terminal:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><span class="strong-term">Node.js version check:</span> <code>node -v</code></li>
    <li><span class="strong-term">npm version check:</span> <code>npm -v</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step 2.2: Extract / Navigate to Workspace</h2>
  <p>Open your terminal, command line, or terminal in VS Code, and navigate to the project directory:</p>
  <p style="font-family: Consolas, monospace; background-color: #f8fafc; padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1;">cd /path/to/school-portal</p>

  <h2>Step 2.3: Install Dependencies</h2>
  <p>To install all frontend and backend dependencies, run:</p>
  <p style="font-family: Consolas, monospace; background-color: #f8fafc; padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1;">npm install</p>
  <p>This command installs required packages, including Express, Multer, xlsx (SheetJS), React, React Router DOM, Recharts, and Lucide React icons.</p>

  <h2>Step 2.4: Running the Servers</h2>
  <p>The project requires running both the React frontend Vite development server and the Node.js Express server:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><span class="strong-term">Frontend Dev Server:</span> Run <code>npm run dev</code> in the root workspace folder. This compiles the React modules and launches the local web client interface at <code>http://localhost:5173</code>.</li>
    <li><span class="strong-term">Backend API Server:</span> Run <code>npm run server</code> (or run <code>node server/index.js</code> directly) in the root workspace folder. This initiates the Express server listening on <code>http://localhost:5000</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  
  <div class="note">
    <strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong> Both commands should run simultaneously. You can open two terminal windows or run them in background processes. In production, building is executed via <code>npm run build</code> and served from the <code>dist</code> directory by Node.js.
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 3 -->
